msgid "Work on Tickets"
msgstr "Рад на тикетима"

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:105
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "How to assign somebody to a ticket?"
msgstr "Ваши додељени тикети"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:109
msgid ""
"In the ticket sidebar tab, you can find an **Owner** field. Choose from the "
"offered agents and make sure to leave an internal note so the other agent "
"knows what it is about."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:112
msgid ""
"If you only have a question or need some information, you could also just "
"[mention a colleague](advanced-features#mention-a-colleague) in an article "
"by using [[@]][[@]] and raise your question."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to delete a ticket?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:117
msgid ""
"First of all, tickets can't be deleted by agents. This is done for the "
"reason of transparency and to prevent deletion by accident and arbitrary "
"deletion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:120
msgid ""
"However, if customers want their data to be deleted (e.g. due to a GDPR "
"deletion request), this can be done in Zammad.  Contact your Zammad admin "
"and ask to execute the deletion job."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:121
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "How to use text templates?"
msgstr "Користите текстуалне шаблоне"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:125
msgid ""
"Use Zammad's [text modules](advanced-features#text-modules) by typing [[:]]"
"[[:]] in the article editor or choose it from the editor toolbar. If you "
"need to have additional modules, ask your Zammad admin to add it for you."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to ask a colleague for help in the ticket?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/faq.md:131
msgid ""
"The best way to do this is to [mention a colleague](advanced-"
"features#mention-a-colleague) in an article by using [[@]][[@]] and raise "
"your question. This triggers a notification for your colleague. Depending on "
"your internal processes, switching the owner of the ticket could also be a "
"possible option."
