msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:56
msgid ""
"The editor **toolbar** includes buttons for common formatting tasks. "
"Hovering over each button will display a tooltip explaining its function. As "
"an alternative you can use **keyboard shortcuts** (see next two sections). "
"For both variants you can activate a formatting option in advance and then "
"add your text or select existing text and apply the formatting option "
"afterwards."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:57
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "General Keyboard Shortcuts"
msgstr "Пречице на тастатури"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:61
msgid ""
"The editor also supports keyboard shortcuts to streamline your workflow. "
"These shortcuts are common across many text processing tools. Important "
"shortcuts are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Shortcut/command              | Formatting\n"
"-------------------------------|---------------\n"
"[[ctrl]] + [[b]]               | **Bold**\n"
"[[ctrl]] + [[i]]               | _Italics_\n"
"[[ctrl]] + [[u]]               | <u>Underline</u>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:70
msgid ""
"Have a look at the next section to use even more formatting via keyboard. "
"Regardless if you are used to Markdown or not, some of them might still be "
"helpful in your daily work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "Markdown Usage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:76
msgid ""
"For users familiar with Markdown syntax, the editor provides support for "
"formatting content with Markdown. When using Markdown syntax, it gets "
"immediately replaced/executed so you can see the result directly in the "
"editor. To go back to standard text, simply use the same limiter again or "
"use [[enter]], depending on the option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:80
msgid ""
"It is not intended to support all Markdown features, but to help users "
"getting things done more easily. Therefore, the most important things are "
"supported like headings, lists, links, code blocks and more. Have a look at "
"the non-exhaustive formatting examples below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/editor.md:89
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Markdown Syntax                | Formatting\n"
"-------------------------------|---------------\n"
"`**`                           | Limiter for **bold**\n"
"`_`                            | Limiter for _italics_\n"
"`#`, `##`, `###`               | Heading, level depending on number of `#`\n"
"`>`                            | Quoted\n"
"`` ` ``                        | Limiter for `inline code`\n"
"`` ``` ``                      | Code block\n"
"`---`                          | Horizontal line as divider\n"
msgstr ""

