msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr "Синтакса"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:50
msgid "Search for a ticket of a specific customer:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (plain)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "customer.firstname: John\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:56
msgid "or:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (plain)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "customer.lastname: Doe\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combining Search Phrases"
msgstr "Комбиновање фраза за претрагу"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:65
msgid ""
"You can combine search phrases by using `AND`, `OR` and `TO` and even "
"separate them with `()`. If you want to exclude search results, you can use "
"negation `!`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Search phrase                                                                               | Description                                                                                                       |\n"
"|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| state.name:(closed OR open) AND (priority.name:\"2 normal\" OR tags:feedback)                 | Show every ticket that state is either closed or open and has priority normal or the tag feedback.                |\n"
"| state.name:(closed OR open) AND (priority.name:\"2 normal\" OR tags:feedback) AND !(_Zammad_) | This gets the same result as above, expect that we don't want the ticket to contain anything matching to \"Zammad\" |\n"
"| owner.email:<bob@example.net> AND state.name:(open OR new)                                  | Show Tickets from <bob@example.net> that are either open or new                                                   |\n"
"| state.name:pending\\* AND article_count:\\[1 TO 5\\]                                           | Show everything with any pending state and an article count of 1 to 5.                                            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional Examples"
msgstr "Додатни примери"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/search.md:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Attribute     | possible Values                       | Example                                                                                        | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n"
"|---------------|---------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n"
"| number        | 1118566                               | number:1118566 number:11185\\*                                                                  | Search for a ticket number                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |\n"
"| title         | some title                            | title:\"some title\" title:Printer title: \"some ti\\*\"                                            | If you need to use spacings in the search phrase, use quotes. Zammad will do a AND-Search over the given words. You can also use a single keyword without quotation.                                                                                 |\n"
"| created_at    | 2018-11-18                            | created_at:2018-11-18 created_at:\\[2018-11-15 TO 2018-11-18\\] created_at:\\>now-1h              | You can either use a simple date, a date-range or \\>now-xh. Please note that the date format needs to be YYYY-MM-DD                                                                                                                                  |\n"
"| state.name    | new open closed                       | state.name: new state.name:new OR open                                                         | You can filter for specific ticket states (and even combine them with an OR). Please note that you need to use the english namings for states, unless you have custom ticket states defined in your instance.                                        |\n"
"| article_count | 5 \\[5 TO 10\\] \\[5 TO \\*\\] \\[\\* TO 5\\] | article_count:5 article_count: \\[5 TO 10\\] article_count:\\[5 TO \\*\\] article_count:\\[\\* TO 5\\] | You can search for Tickets with a specific number of articles (you can even search for everything with 5 or more articles or even up to 5 articles, if needed).                                                                                      |\n"
"| article.from  | \\*bob\\*                               | article.from:\\*bob\\*                                                                           | Show all tickets that contain articles from \"Bob\"                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n"
"| article.body  | heat heat~ /joh?n(ath\\[oa\\]n)/        | article.body:heat article.body:heat~ articlebody:/joh?n(ath\\[oa\\]n)/                           | First example shows every ticket containing the word \"heat\" - you can also use the fuzzy operator \"~\" to search for similar words like e.g. like \"head\". Zammad will also allow you to use regular expressions, where ever the attributes allows it. |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two-Factor Authentication"
msgstr "Двофакторска аутентификација"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:12
msgid ""
"Two-factor authentication (2FA) enhances the security of your Zammad account "
"by adding an extra layer of verification beyond a password. It requires you "
"to provide two different types of authentication factors, typically "
"something you know (like a password) and something you possess (like a "
"mobile device or a security token), to ensure that you are an authorized "
"individual who can access the account."
msgstr ""
"Двофакторска аутентификација (2FA) повишава безбедност вашег Zammad налога "
"додавањем додатног слоја верификације поред лозинке. Захтева од вас да "
"обезбедите два различита фактора за аутентификацију, обично нешто што знате "
"(попут лозинке) и нешто што поседујете (као што је мобилни уређај или "
"безбедносни кључ), да би потвдили да сте овлашћена особа која може да "
"приступи налогу."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:16
msgid ""
"Two-Factor Authentication is an **optional feature**. Administrators must "
"activate it to be visible in your profile settings. The 2FA usage may be "
"even enforced by your admin. In this case, you can't use Zammad unless you "
"set up at least one 2FA method."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set Up"
msgstr "Поставка"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the system admin has enabled this feature, you can head to _Avatar > Profile > Two-factor Authentication_ to set it\n"
"up. Depending on the enabled two-factor methods, you may see one or more options in the table.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:23
msgid ""
"To set up a two-factor method, use the ::+:: button and follow the steps."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:25
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows 2FA methods in user profile settings](/screenshots/"
"cypress/usage-guide-2fa.cy.js/2fa-methods-profile-setup.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Пример снимка екрана (пуна страна)](/screenshots/cypress/test.cy.js/test-"
"screenshot-full-page.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:27
msgid "In a modal dialog, you will be asked to confirm your current password."
msgstr "У дијалогу ћете бити упитани да потврдите вашу тренутну лозинку."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:30
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Depending on the chosen two-factor method, you will be guided through the "
"setup process, which includes specific steps.  Continue with using an "
"[Authentication App](#authentication-app) or a [Security Key](#security-key)."
msgstr ""
"У зависности од изабраног метода двофакторске аутентификације, бићете поново "
"вођени кроз процес постављања. Обично ће уређивање методе једноставно "
"обновити и заменити старију поставку, али неке методе подржавају и напредне "
"функције (нпр. додавање више безбедносних кључева)."

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication App"
msgstr "Апликација за аутентификацију"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:36
msgid ""
"The authenticator app method is a type of two-factor authentication that "
"uses a mobile application to generate one-time codes for account "
"verification. After setting up the authenticator app on your device, you "
"will link it to your Zammad account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:38
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows app authentication configuration](/screenshots/two-factor-"
"auth-usage/2fa-app-setup.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Пример снимка екрана (пуна страна)](/screenshots/cypress/test.cy.js/test-"
"screenshot-full-page.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:40
msgid ""
"First, make sure you have installed an authenticator app on your mobile "
"device. Recommended apps are:"
msgstr ""
"Прво, проверите да ли сте инсталирали апликацију за аутентификацију на свом "
"мобилном уређају. Препоручене апликације су:"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:44
msgid ""
"[Google Authenticator](https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/1066447)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:44
msgid ""
"[Authy](https://support.authy.com/hc/en-us/articles/115001945848-Installing-"
"Authy-apps/)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:44
msgid ""
"[Microsoft Authenticator](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/account-"
"billing/download-and-install-the-microsoft-authenticator-"
"app-351498fc-850a-45da-b7b6-27e523b8702a)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:47
msgid ""
"Next, open the authenticator app on your device and find a **Scan QR Code** "
"action, or similar. Point your camera to the Zammad screen and scan the "
"shown QR code in the middle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your device is not able to scan the QR code, first click on it to reveal your secret. Next, add a manual entry to\n"
"your authenticator app and enter the provided secret when asked.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:55
msgid ""
"Your authenticator app should immediately add the new entry for your Zammad "
"account, and a 6-digit code will be displayed next to it together with a "
"timer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:58
msgid ""
"Back in Zammad, enter the provided code to the **Security Code** field and "
"click on **Set Up**. Go on either by setting up another 2FA method "
"([security key](#security-key)) or check how to [log in with 2FA](#sign-in)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "Security Key"
msgstr "Безбедносни кључ"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:64
msgid ""
"The security keys method is a type of a two-factor authentication that uses "
"Web Authentication API in the browser for verifying your identity. You may "
"register multiple hardware or software security keys with your Zammad "
"account and then they can be used during the sign-in process."
msgstr ""
"Метод безбедносних кључева је врста двофакторске аутентификације која "
"користи Web Authentication API претраживача за верификацију вашег "
"идентитета. Можете да региструјете више хардверских или софтверских "
"безбедносних кључева са својим Zammad налогом, а затим их можете користити "
"током процеса пријављивања."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:66
msgid ""
"Initially, you will be presented with an empty side panel instructing you to "
"**Set Up** your first key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:68
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows security key authentication configuration](/screenshots/"
"two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-security-key-panel.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Пример снимка екрана (пуна страна)](/screenshots/cypress/test.cy.js/test-"
"screenshot-full-page.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:71
msgid ""
"Then, enter a descriptive **Name for this security key** you will be "
"registering with your account, so you could later identify it in the list. "
"Then, click on **Next**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:74
msgid ""
"Next, depending you your browser, you will be presented with different "
"options. Select one that refers to your chosen security key and follow the "
"instructions on the screen."
msgstr ""
"Затим, у зависности од вашег претраживача, биће вам представљене различите "
"опције. Изаберите ону која се односи на жељени безбедносни кључ и пратите "
"упутства на екрану."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:76
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows security key authentication configuration](/screenshots/"
"two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-passkey-auth.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Пример снимка екрана (пуна страна)](/screenshots/cypress/test.cy.js/test-"
"screenshot-full-page.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:79
msgid ""
"You may be asked by the browser to interact with a key or a device so you "
"can prove you are in physical possession of it (e.g. enter its PIN to unlock "
"it)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You will have limited time (measured in tens of seconds) to register your key. Better to have it ready before you\n"
"proceed!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:87
msgid ""
"If the registration was successful, the modal dialog will close and you are "
"good to go. In case of errors, you will be able to **Retry** the "
"registration of the key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:89
msgid ""
"Once set up, security keys can be managed by choosing **Edit** action next "
"to the two-factor authentication method."
msgstr ""
"Када се подесе, безбедносним кључевима се може управљати тако што ћете "
"изабрати акцију **Измени** поред метода редакторске аутентификације."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:93
msgid ""
"You have an option to remove a key or set up additional ones. There is no "
"limit in number of security keys you can set up, but keep in mind you cannot "
"register an already registered key for your account. Removal of the last "
"security key will effectively remove the complete security keys method for "
"your account."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:94
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sign-in"
msgstr "Пријава"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:99
msgid ""
"When you set up two-factor authentication for your Zammad account, during "
"the next sign-in you will be asked to provide the same two-factor method "
"after entering correct username and password. Depending on the chosen two-"
"factor method, this may be a security code, hardware key, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:102
msgid ""
"In case you are having issues during sign-in with your preferred two-factor "
"authentication method, you can switch to another one, provided you have set "
"it up previously."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:105
msgid ""
"Look for **Try another method** link below the sign in box. In case you "
"don't see this link, you probably have no other available two-factor methods "
"set up, or your admin has disabled this feature."
msgstr ""
"Потражите линк **Покушајте други метод** испод прозора за пријаву. У случају "
"да не видите овај линк, вероватно немате подешене друге доступне методе "
"двофакторске аутентификације или је ваш администратор онемогућио ову "
"функцију."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:107
msgid ""
"![Log in screen with link to \"Try another method\"](/screenshots/two-factor-"
"auth-usage/2fa-link-another-method.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:111
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also use one of your recovery codes, which are auto-"
"generated for your account during the initial setup of the two-factor "
"authentication. Click on **Or use one of your recovery codes**, enter one of "
"your unused codes and click on **Sign in**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:113
msgid ""
"![Log in screen with recovery codes link](/screenshots/two-factor-auth-usage/"
"2fa-login-recovery-codes.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use a single recovery code only once! In case you exhaust the list of your recovery codes, it is recommended\n"
"you regenerate them for your account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:119
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate Recovery Codes"
msgstr "Генерисање шифри за опоравак"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:123
msgid ""
"Recovery codes are one-time use security codes that can be used to sign in "
"if you lose access to your other two-factor authentication methods. They can "
"only be used as a **backup method**."
msgstr ""
"Шифре за опоравак су једнократни безбедносни кодови који се могу користити "
"за пријављивање ако изгубите приступ другим методама двофакторске "
"аутентификације. Могуће их је користити само као **резервни метод**."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:126
msgid ""
"If the feature is enabled by the admin, recovery codes will be automatically "
"generated for you during the setup of your initial two-factor authentication "
"method."
msgstr ""
"Ако је администратор омогућио ову функцију, шифре за опоравак ће бити "
"аутоматски генерисане за вас током постављања вашег почетног метода "
"двофакторске аутентификације."

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:129
msgid ""
"You will be asked to print out or save the generated recovery codes in a "
"safe place. Once used, a recovery code cannot be reused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:131
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows output of recovery codes during 2FA setup](/screenshots/"
"two-factor-auth-usage/2fa-app-setup-recovery-codes.png)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:135
msgid ""
"You also have an option to regenerate your recovery codes at any time, which "
"invalidates already existing recovery codes and provides you with a list of "
"fresh codes. You can do this by clicking on `Regenerate recovery codes` "
"button in your profile's 2FA settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set a Default 2FA Method"
msgstr "Постављање подразумеваног метода двофакторске аутентификације"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:140
msgid ""
"To set an already set up two-factor method as default, use the ::a:: actions "
"menu next to it in your profile's 2FA settings and choose **Set as default**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:143
msgid ""
"In order to identify your current default two-factor authentication method, "
"look for a small blue badge next to the method name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:145
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows list of 2FA methods and default method](/screenshots/"
"cypress/usage-guide-2fa.cy.js/2fa-methods-profile-overview.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Снимак екрана који приказује пројекте превода у Weblate менију](/"
"screenshots/weblate-overview-docs.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:148
msgid ""
"A default two-factor authentication method is just your preferred method "
"during the sign-in process. You will always have an option to try signing in "
"using another method."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:149
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edit a 2FA Method"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:152
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"![Screenshot shows the action menu for an already set up 2FA method](/"
"screenshots/cypress/usage-guide-2fa.cy.js/2fa-methods-profile-action-"
"menu.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Пример снимка екрана (пуна страна)](/screenshots/cypress/test.cy.js/test-"
"screenshot-full-page.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:155
msgid ""
"To edit an already set up two-factor method, use the ::a:: actions menu next "
"to it and choose **Edit**. In a modal dialog, you will be asked to confirm "
"your current password."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:159
msgid ""
"Depending on the chosen two-factor method, you will be guided again through "
"the setup process. Normally, editing a method will simply renew it and "
"replace the older setup, but some methods do support advanced functions "
"(e.g. adding multiple security keys)."
msgstr ""
"У зависности од изабраног метода двофакторске аутентификације, бићете поново "
"вођени кроз процес постављања. Обично ће уређивање методе једноставно "
"обновити и заменити старију поставку, али неке методе подржавају и напредне "
"функције (нпр. додавање више безбедносних кључева)."

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove a 2FA Method"
msgstr "Уклањање метода двофакторске аутентификације"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/guides/two-factor-auth.md:163
msgid ""
"To remove an already set up two-factor method, use the ::a:: actions menu "
"next to it and choose **Remove**. In a modal dialog, you will be asked to "
"confirm the removal with your current password."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage Your User Profile"
msgstr "Управљање вашим корисничким профилом"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/documentation/use/manage-profile.md:9
#, fuzzy
