msgid "CTI"
msgstr "CTI"

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic CTI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:11
msgid "This page describes the generic CTI API scopes and functionalities."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"- Authentication on this endpoint works fundamentally different compared to\n"
"  the rest of the API.\n"
"- API clients _do not_ work with the CTI endpoints unless explicitly stated\n"
"  by the client vendor!\n"
"- The CTI endpoints are relevant for PBX systems only.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:25
msgid ""
"Here's a small condensed list of the possibilities this CTI API provides."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:26 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:166
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:322 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:440
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inbound"
msgstr "Долазнo"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:30 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:35
msgid "Caller log functions for your agents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:30
msgid "Blocking of caller IDs during signaling."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:31 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:123
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:279 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:397
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outbound"
msgstr "Одлазнo"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:35
msgid "Set outbound caller IDs depending on the caller ID target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:41
msgid ""
"The endpoint can be found in the generic CTI integration and contains a "
"unique token which acts as authentication. Make sure to keep this endpoint "
"URL safe."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (info)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generic CTI configuration and the correct endpoint can be found in your\n"
"Zammad in the admin interface under _System > Integrations > CTI (generic)_.\n"
"\n"
"Please also note the there listed requirements and limitations.\n"
"All options that require returns (e.g. blocking, manipulating outgoing\n"
"caller IDs) rely on configurations within the Zammad CTI integration\n"
"page.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are two options how to `POST` the relevant data to Zammad:\n"
"\n"
"- JSON (recommended)\n"
"- Form-data\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:63
msgid ""
"There are several events in terms of an ongoing call. These actions always "
"come from your PBX system and may be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:67
msgid "\"newCall\" event (initiation of a call)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:67
msgid "\"hangup\" event (call ending)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:67
msgid "\"answer\" event (aka picking up the phone)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:72
msgid ""
"In some situations Zammad may provide a return on your PBX calls (e.g. a "
"reject) if you blocked a specific caller. Zammad will never initiate "
"specific actions with your PBX. Zammad is a passive component in all "
"described cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "Used Examples"
msgstr "Коришћени примери"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example:**\n"
"Below calls have been sent with the following configuration. This is\n"
"important for you to understand the responses we are showing here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Outbound:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:85
msgid ""
"Destination caller ID `4989*` set outbound caller ID `498999998145` with "
"note \"All from munich\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:85
msgid ""
"Destination caller ID `4930*` set outbound caller ID `493023125877` \"All "
"from Berlin\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Other settings:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:89
msgid "Default caller ID for outbound calls `496990009111`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "New Call Event"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:95 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "Available `attributes` and <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"sample data\" />:\n"
msgstr "Доступни `атрибути` и <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"примери\" />:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`event` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"newCall\"/>\n"
": Tell Zammad there is a new call.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`from` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"4930555716000\"/>\n"
": Number that initiated the call. Can be `anonymous` as well.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:104
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`to` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"4930555716000\"/>\n"
": Number that is being called.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`direction` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"in\"/>\n"
": The call direction. If your agent initiates a call, this will be `out`. Calls\n"
"from external side to you are `in`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`callId` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"53ba82e2bd6d12d9fb2d3838f0cfb070\"/>\n"
": An ID that is unique for the call. Zammad will use this ID to identify an\n"
"  existing call with following actions (e.g. like answering or hanging up).\n"
